## 5. VFX: how to build each part
Layer roles: every part is FLASH, MAIN, SECONDARY or RESIDUAL. Each gets its own CONFIG block. Nothing pops in or out; everything scales or fades in and out.

| Time | Layer | Role | How to build it |
|---|---|---|---|
| F4–F8 | Hand crackle | SECONDARY | 2–3 short procedural bolts (see "Procedural lightning" below), 0.6 studs long, around the RightHand attachment, plus 4 tiny sparks. |
| F8 | Spear forms | MAIN | The spear grows from the hand: Size tweens from length 0 to 6 studs over 4 frames, Quint Out, starting from the grip. |
| F8–flight | Spear core | MAIN | Blender mesh: long diamond-tipped lance with a tapered tail, under 100 tris, UV running along its length. In Roblox: MeshPart, Neon material, colour #FFFDF0, plus an inner Beam along its length using a white-to-transparent gradient texture for the glow edge. |
| F8–flight | Crossed ribbons | MAIN | Blender mesh: a DOUBLE HELIX of 2 thin flat ribbons, 1.5 turns over the spear length, radius 0.4, tapering at both ends, UV along each ribbon. In Roblox: MeshPart, Neon, colour #FFE14D, transparency 0.2, spinning around the spear axis at 4 turns/s. Its texture fades out at both ends. |
| F15 | Release flash | FLASH | 8-point star texture on a BillboardGui or ParticleEmitter :Emit(1) at the hand, 5 studs, gone within 0.08 s. Plus a PointLight (#FFE14D, range 14) fading to 0 in 0.15 s. Small camera shake for the thrower only. |
| Flight | Glow light | SECONDARY | A PointLight on the spear: range 12, brightness 2, colour #FFE14D. |
| Flight | Crackling trail | MAIN | Procedural lightning: a bolt from the spear's tail back along the flight path, 10–14 studs long, 10 segments, regenerated every 2 frames. Old bolts fade over 0.1 s. Plus a Roblox Trail on the spear: wind-streak texture, lifetime 0.15 s, width 0.6→0. |
| Flight | Shed sparks | RESIDUAL | ParticleEmitter on the spear: about 40/s, Squash for streaks, speed 2–6, lifetime 0.25 s, colour #FFE14D with a few #9FD8FF. |
| Hit | Impact flash | FLASH | Star flash 8 studs, 0.08 s, plus a PointLight burst (range 20, 0.2 s). |
| Hit | Spark burst | MAIN | ParticleEmitter :Emit(40): speed 30–50, Drag 6, small gravity, Squash, lifetime 0.3–0.5 s. Plus 5–6 short procedural bolts (2–4 studs) shooting outward from the hit point, 0.12 s each. |
| Hit | Shock ring | SECONDARY | A thin ring mesh (Blender, UV around the ring) facing the thrower, scaling 1→6 studs over 0.2 s while fading. |
| +0.0–0.6 s | Electric arcs on target | RESIDUAL | 2–3 small bolts jumping between random limb attachments on the target, regenerated every 3 frames. |
| +0.0–2.0 s | Scorch mark | RESIDUAL | Raycast down from the hit point to the floor and place a Decal (scorch texture) on a thin anchored part there. It fades over the last 1 s. Skip it if there is no floor within 6 studs. |

### Procedural lightning (write it once, reuse it everywhere)
- Write ONE module, LightningBolt, that takes (startPos, endPos, segments, maxOffset, thickness, colour, lifetime).
- Points: evenly spaced along the line. Each middle point gets a random sideways offset, up to maxOffset (default 0.6 studs). Offsets are smaller near the two ends, so the bolt stays attached.
- Each segment is a Beam between two Attachments: texture a soft-edged white line, LightEmission 1, FaceCamera true, Width0/Width1 = thickness, Segments 1. Keep the Attachments on one anchored holder part. Reuse instances through a pool; don't Instance.new them every frame.
- Optional: 1 small branch per bolt at a random middle point, 30–50% of the length.
- An open-source reference exists: the "Lightning Beams" module by SamyBlue (link at the bottom). Only copy from it if its repository has a license file that allows reuse, and tell me which license. Otherwise write your own using the rules above.

### Blender assets (meshes and textures)
- Meshes: spear_core, ribbon_helix, shock_ring. Under 400 triangles total. Origins: the spear's grip point and the ring's centre. Apply transforms. Export each one separately.
- Textures: white/greyscale on a transparent background; colour is added in Roblox. Render with an orthographic camera, Film Transparent, Standard view transform (not AgX/Filmic).
  - star_flash.png (512)
  - spark.png (256)
  - glow_line.png (512×128, for the Beams)
  - streak.png (512)
  - scorch.png (512: dark centre, cracks, soft edge, coloured dark grey)
- Check every texture on dark AND light backgrounds, and check for halo edges (white fringes).

### Roblox rules
- ParticleEmitters: Enabled false, use :Emit(). Size and Transparency curves have at least 3 points. Use ZOffset for layer order.
- MeshParts and helper parts: Anchored, CanCollide/CanQuery/CanTouch false, CastShadow false.
- Every time value is multiplied by CONFIG.TIME_SCALE.
- Budget per cast: at most 150 particles alive, 30 Beams, 20 other instances. Disable bolts more than 200 studs from the camera.
- Don't change the global Lighting (Bloom etc.) without asking me. Tell me if Bloom would help.

